    {
      "slug": "artifacts/the-silence-engine",
      "type": "artifact",
      "tension": 0.86,
      "facts": {
        "archetype": "weapon-relic",
        "maker": "the-velt",
        "note": "Kael's deathbed dampener, built to mute the wound; it works once, then returns what it swallowed twice as loud"
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-marrow-was-alive",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.7,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "step": "1-cause",
        "text": "The dark ore the Velt mined was never mineral. It was the dormant nerve-marrow of a single planet-spanning organism, asleep since before the suns cooled."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/extraction-was-amputation",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "step": "2-escalation",
        "text": "Every bore-shaft severed living tissue. The world did not die; it woke, in pieces, in pain, and began to dream of the things cutting into it."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-wound-sang",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.8,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "step": "3-escalation",
        "text": "The severed marrow discharged its agony as a psychic standing-wave. The Choir heard it first and could not stop hearing it; the Pale Wing read it as profit and sold it."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-choir-tried-to-sing-it-down",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.85,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "step": "4-point-of-no-return",
        "text": "The Choir threw its entire gestalt against the wound, singing a counter-wave to lull the planet back to sleep. Instead the planet learned the Choir's frequency and answered in their own voices."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-psychic-cascade",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.9,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "step": "5-collapse",
        "text": "The amplified wave reached the seams under every city at once. The Velt vitrified mid-thought, the Choir dissolved into the song, the Pale Wing fled into the dark, and three empires ended in a single shared instant of the planet's pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/velt-thought-in-stone",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.52,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The Velt did not write; they thought into silicate across centuries. To read their glass is to overhear a single hundred-year sentence."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/marrow-quickened-the-velt",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.6,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "Refined marrow let a Velt think in days instead of decades. Their golden age was an addiction, and the bores were the needle."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-marrow-remembers-the-cut",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.85,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The shard is not dead tissue. It is awake, it remembers being severed, and held long enough it teaches the holder to hear the planet whether they want to or not."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-shard-wants-reunion",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.82,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "Every fragment of marrow strains toward the vein. Reunite enough of it and the organism wakes whole, and the colony sits on the largest seam left."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-last-warning",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.84,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The Cantor's final loop is not grief. Decoded, it is an instruction in three words: do not dig, do not sing, let it sleep."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-counter-wave-failed",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The fork's vibration is the Choir's lullaby preserved. Played near the wound it does not soothe; the planet sings it back, perfected and predatory."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-pale-wing-knew-and-sold-it",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.74,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The ledger proves the Pale Wing saw the cascade coming with years to spare and chose to auction the ending rather than avert it. Their unsold last entry is dated the day of the waking."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/every-city-sat-on-a-seam",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.7,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The vitrified map proves the Velt built atop the marrow on purpose, for proximity sped their thoughts. They paved their own graves to think faster."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-seams-run-under-the-colony",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.8,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The largest unbroken seam on the map runs directly beneath Colony Drosselmeyer, and the drill is already pointed at it."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/silence-is-borrowed",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.8,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The Silence Engine buys quiet by storing the wound's song. Its capacity is finite, and what it holds it eventually returns, louder than it took."
      }
    },
